 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "감정 형용사: bored / boring · interested / interesting",
   "en": "feelings: -ed and -ing adjectives"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "감정을 나타내는 형용사는 -ed와 -ing 두 형태가 있습니다. -ed 형용사는 사람이 느끼는 감정을 말하고(I'm bored. She was interested.), -ing 형용사는 감정을 일으키는 사람이나 사물의 성질을 말합니다(The film was boring. It was an interesting book.). 전치사는 형용사마다 달라서 함께 외워 두세요: interested in, surprised at / by, disappointed with / by, bored with.",
   "en": "Adjectives about feelings have an -ed form and an -ing form. Use -ed to say how a person feels (I'm bored. She was interested.) and -ing to describe what causes the feeling (The film was boring. It was an interesting book.). Prepositions go with particular adjectives, so learn them together: interested in, surprised at / by, disappointed with / by, bored with."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "구조 / Structure",
    "형태 / Form",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "감정 / feeling",
     "-ed adjective",
     "I was bored by the film."
    ],
    [
     "원인 / cause",
     "-ing adjective",
     "The film was boring."
    ],
    [
     "전치사 / preposition",
     "interested in · surprised at · disappointed with",
     "I'm interested in history."
    ],
    [
     "강조 / intensifier",
     "really · very · quite + adjective",
     "It was really exciting."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "사람에게는 보통 -ed, 사물이나 상황에는 -ing를 씁니다.",
    "en": "People usually take -ed, things and situations take -ing."
   },
   {
    "ko": "I'm boring.은 '나는 지루한 사람이다'라는 뜻이므로 주의하세요.",
    "en": "I'm boring means I'm a boring person; use I'm bored for the feeling."
   },
   {
    "ko": "surprised, shocked, excited 등은 대부분 같은 방식으로 만듭니다.",
    "en": "Surprised, shocked, excited and many others work the same way."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
